# Patrick's dotfiles

These are my dotfiles.  There are many like them, but these are mine.

They are mostly for ZSH and Mac, but I use them on Linux too.  I use oh-my-zsh (https://github.com/ohmyzsh/ohmyzsh).

## Installation and Usage

Clone this repo to `~/dotfiles` (the shell configs expect it there), then run
`script/install`:

    git clone git@github.com:PatrickTulskie/dotfiles.git ~/dotfiles
    ~/dotfiles/script/install

`script/install` is idempotent and safe to re-run on any machine. It symlinks
everything into place (backing up anything real it would clobber), installs
oh-my-zsh, vim-plug and the Meslo Nerd Font if they're missing, and seeds
Rectangle's prefs on a machine that has none yet.

## Layout

    zsh/zshrc         symlinked to ~/.zshrc
    zsh/path.zsh      the only place PATH is assembled
    zsh/env.zsh       exports
    zsh/aliases.zsh   aliases
    zsh/linux.zsh     Linux-only bits
    bin/              scripts, on PATH via path.zsh
    config/           app configs symlinked into ~/.config (git, ghostty, ...)
    private/_*        gitignored; anything matching is sourced after the rest

If you'd rather not run the installer, source `zsh/path.zsh` before oh-my-zsh
and the other `zsh/*.zsh` files after it, as `zsh/zshrc` does.

## Notes

`config/git/config` is linked to `~/.gitconfig`, so `git config --global`
writes land in the repo. `config/git/ignore` goes to `~/.config/git/ignore`,
git's default global excludes path.

`config/hunk/config.toml` defines a "Monokai Soda" custom theme for
[hunk](https://github.com/modem-dev/hunk) that matches the Ghostty terminal
theme (hunk ships plain Monokai but no Soda variant).

`config/herdr/config.toml` does the same for [herdr](https://herdr.dev) via its
`[theme.custom]` token overrides, using the same palette.

`zsh/zshrc` binds ctrl+r to [atuin](https://atuin.sh) via `--disable-up-arrow`,
so history search is atuin's but up-arrow stays zsh's. The binary comes from
Homebrew (see the `iac` repo); the hook is guarded on `command -v atuin`, so a
box without it just falls back to zsh's own ctrl+r. `config/atuin/config.toml`
keeps it local-only — no account, no sync, no network.

`fuck` is [pay-respects](https://github.com/iffse/pay-respects), also from
Homebrew and also guarded, so it's simply absent where it isn't installed.

fzf is deliberately *not* wired into the shell. It's installed for vim's
`<C-P>` (`:FZF`), which only needs the binary on PATH, and atuin owns ctrl+r.

cmd+k clears the screen inside herdr panes (and any other TUI) because
`config/ghostty/config` remaps it to send ctrl+l rather than firing Ghostty's
own `clear_screen`. Ghostty's scrollback-wiping clear moved to cmd+shift+k.

`config/rectangle/RectangleConfig.json` only seeds a fresh machine. To update
it, export from Rectangle's settings and overwrite the file.

`config/iterm` and `resources/themes/macos-terminal` are kept for reference but
nothing installs them; Ghostty is the terminal.
